/// The headline figures for a reader who wants the answer and not the plumbing: outturn, plan, variance on the plan's basis, the group income and expenditure statement, outturn on the current department structure, and each of them in 2025-26 prices, with the year, period, department and Spending Review group to cut them by and the three calculation groups. No keys, no quarantine tables, no restatement detail. A perspective narrows the field list and secures nothing.
perspective Executive

	perspectiveTable 'Fiscal Year'

		perspectiveColumn 'Financial Year'

	perspectiveTable 'Fiscal Period'

		perspectiveColumn 'Period Number'

		perspectiveColumn Period

		perspectiveColumn Month

		perspectiveColumn 'Month Start Date'

		perspectiveColumn 'Fiscal Quarter'

		perspectiveColumn 'Is Period 0'

	perspectiveTable 'Department (current structure)'

		perspectiveColumn Department

		perspectiveColumn 'Department Number'

		perspectiveColumn 'Department Type'

		perspectiveColumn 'Valid From Release'

		perspectiveColumn 'Valid To Release'

	perspectiveTable 'Spending Review Group'

		perspectiveColumn 'Spending Review Group'

		perspectiveColumn 'Group Code'

		perspectiveColumn 'Member Type'

		perspectiveColumn 'Is Department Group'

		perspectiveColumn 'Has Outturn'

		perspectiveColumn 'Group Description'

	perspectiveTable 'Statement Line'

		perspectiveColumn Line

		perspectiveColumn 'Line (indented)'

		perspectiveColumn 'Line Id'

		perspectiveColumn 'Line Type'

		perspectiveColumn 'Sign Presentation'

		perspectiveColumn 'Indent Level'

		perspectiveColumn 'Plan Scope'

		perspectiveColumn Members

	perspectiveTable 'Time Intelligence'

		perspectiveColumn 'Time Calculation'

	perspectiveTable 'Scenario Comparison'

		perspectiveColumn Comparison

	perspectiveTable 'Display Unit'

		perspectiveColumn Unit

